    "collapsible_text_YPVYyd": {
      "type": "collapsible-text",
      "settings": {
        "richtext": "<p>When choosing the right mats for a car there is a lot to weigh up. Anyone unfamiliar with the subject may struggle to buy products that meet expectations and stay reliable in every situation. Finding the ideal mats for a specific make of car is hard too.</p><p>Unfortunately, some sets do not fit well enough or fall short in everyday use. Below we describe rubber car mats and compare them with our innovative EVA products. You will see for yourself how good our product is — and EVA mats will soon be in your car!</p>",
        "collapsible_richtext": "<h3>What are rubber mats and where does their popularity come from?</h3><p>The popularity of rubber car mats comes from the fact that they are relatively cheap to maintain and universal. They work in every car model and meet most people's expectations. For years they were considered almost indestructible thanks to their exceptional resistance to mechanical damage. They perform well in almost any weather — whether it rains or snows, rubber mats keep the interior clean. They are also very resistant to the chemicals in cleaning products, so looking after them is simple and does not take much time.</p><p></p>",
        "button_text_more": "Read more",
        "button_text_less": "Read less",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 50,
        "padding_bottom": 57
      }
    },
    "image_with_collapsible_text_XCLeBp": {
      "type": "image-with-collapsible-text",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Frame_233.png",
        "header": "<p><strong>What to look for</strong> when choosing mats?</p>",
        "richtext": "<p>If you are considering new car mats and do not know which technical aspects to focus on, we will help. First choose the material. The way they are fixed matters too — some models have no factory fasteners, so pick mats with a set of stoppers. The product must sit tight against the floor and must not slide while driving. The finish should not be an afterthought — if looks matter to you, the mats should match the interior in colour and size. Shape is important as well: mats that are too small slide around, and mats that are too large can catch the pedals — which is dangerous for everyone on board.</p>",
        "collapsible_richtext": "<h3>What types of rubber car mats are there?</h3><p>Car mats fall into two types: tray mats and standard mats. Tray mats have a high edge that stops water spilling into the interior. The drive is safe and you can pour the excess water out easily — just take the mat out. Tray mats with a modern finish are available on the market, which makes them more versatile. Standard rubber mats have a specific pattern that limits the movement of water or mud inside the car and protects the original carpet.</p>",
        "button_text_more": "Read more",
        "button_text_less": "Read less",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 80,
        "padding_bottom": 80
      }
    },
    "text_with_image_zBPL3c": {
      "type": "text-with-image",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Rectangle_91_1.png",
        "header": "<p><strong>How do EVA mats differ</strong> from traditional rubber mats?</p>",
        "richtext": "<p>There are many similarities and differences between traditional rubber mats and EVA products. Let us start with what they have in common.</p><p>Above all, both rubber and EVA mats do not absorb water. Their construction prevents leaking not only on rainy days, but on snowy ones too.</p><p>Both products also work excellently as protection against every kind of dirt, because the material they are made of lets no dirt or liquid through. Rubber car mats, however, do not cover the whole floor — they protect roughly 70–90% of the car's carpet.</p><p>EVA mats are made to measure, which means they protect the largest possible area of the floor. <strong>That is up to 99% coverage!</strong> On top of that, EVA mats are odourless and non-toxic. Traditional rubber mats smell unpleasant and contain toxic substances. Dirt travels across them because it is not absorbed into the material.</p><p>In EVA mats dirt is <strong>trapped in technological cells</strong>. They are also far lighter and therefore easier to take out of the car. They need no special cleaning either.</p>",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 80,
        "padding_bottom": 80
      }
    },
    "richtext_section_K7WAxg": {
      "type": "richtext-section",
      "settings": {
        "header": "<h2>Why is it worth <strong>buying mats in our store?</strong></h2>",
        "richtext": "<p>When you buy EVA mats in our store you get a guarantee of excellent quality at a great price. They are handmade products. We are confident you will be happy with your choice of EVA mats!</p>",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 58,
        "padding_bottom": 57
      }
    },
