    "home_faq_xEmBQm": {
      "type": "home-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "text_DzQCYQ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>Will the mats definitely fit?</p>",
            "des": "<p>Absolutely. We make the mats individually for each car model — taking into account the brand, model, generation, year, gearbox and the specific equipment. They are processed by hand: cut, edged and profiled manually. Our patterns are based solely on measurements we take from physical cars, so there is no room for inaccuracy. The mats cover the whole floor including the small details, reaching places rubber or velour mats can only dream of.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_mX9qEM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>How do I clean them?</p>",
            "des": "<p>Thanks to the technology used, dirt does not soak into the mat and does not stick to it — simply shake the mat out and everything comes off. With heavier mud you can safely wash it with a pressure washer and drive on.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_VPPPMN": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>A mat for the tunnel? What is that?</p>",
            "des": "<p>Carvion mats cover up to 98% of the floor, so we take care of every detail — the rear tunnel is covered too, which keeps the floor clean at all times.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_XjTUky": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>How long will they last?</p>",
            "des": "<p>EVA material is known for its strength and abrasion resistance. It is also used in gyms (as mats under machines) and in footwear (soles). Compared with the alternatives, EVA mats handle wear extremely well, which lets you use them for 5–7 years with no signs of use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_e6APUk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>Classic and 3D — what is the difference?</p>",
            "des": "<p>With both sets we cover as much of the car floor as possible. The 3D set additionally covers the side trim next to the floor and includes more 3D elements (floor contours), which we account for during production so the mats sit perfectly.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_exrU7q": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>What is EVA material?</p>",
            "des": "<p>It is a 10 mm thick foam with 7 mm deep cells, which easily keeps dirt and water in one place — nothing gets under the mat until you shake it out.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_TqKDiD": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>Are EVA mats for summer or for winter?</p>",
            "des": "<p>EVA mats are all-season. They are practical in winter (waterproof, easy to clean, covering up to 98% of the floor) and in summer (odourless, pleasant to the touch, they do not deform in the heat).</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_mqJ6Qk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>What is the delivery time?</p>",
            "des": "<p>It takes roughly 2 weeks from placing the order, because we make the mats to order as they come in. If you own a very unusual car or another vehicle (a motorboat, helicopter, excavator or tractor), the lead time can extend to 4–6 weeks.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_dUePyr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "hd": "<p>How is the delivery handled?</p>",
            "des": "<p>We ship the mats by courier straight to the customer's address. We do not send them to parcel lockers because of the product size. We want the mats to arrive exactly as they were made — we do not fold or bend them, as that could affect how they fit later on.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
